Bug Details
Bug Title	Horse clips through fences when moving diagonally alongside fences
Date Found	27 June 2025
Game Version	Stardew Valley v1.6.15 (Steam, PC)
Tester	Emre Sedef
Description

When riding a horse alongside a fence and moving diagonally (forward + left/right), the horse can clip through the fence geometry and partially or fully enter restricted areas.

This indicates a collision detection issue where diagonal movement vectors do not properly respect fence boundaries. While collisions behave correctly during straight movement (horizontal/vertical), diagonal input bypasses or weakens the collision response.

This may allow unintended map access and breaks environmental consistency.

Steps to Reproduce
Mount the horse
Ride alongside a fence in a straight line
While moving, press forward + left/right to move diagonally toward the fence
Observe the horse’s collision with the fence
Expected Result

The horse should not be able to pass through or clip into fences under any movement direction. Collision detection must fully block movement across fence boundaries.

Actual Result
Horse clips through or partially enters the fence when moving diagonally
Collision is not consistently enforced during diagonal movement
